      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "What is the $4$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=128,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =128 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}(128)=-64 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}(-64)=32 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2}(32)=-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{4}=-16.$",
